[38;5;252m[1m## What the C project does[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;10mc_src[0m is a preprocessor-heavy microbenchmark: [38;5;10mmdmacros.h[0m uses token pasting on the [38;5;10m-DOP=[0m and [38;5;10m-DREPEAT=[0m macros supplied by CMake to pick an operation function ([38;5;10mop_add[0m/[38;5;10mop_sub[0m/[38;5;10mop_mul[0m), an accumulator seed, a per-iteration step, and a manually unrolled [38;5;10mREP0[0m…[38;5;10mREP7[0m chain. [38;5;10mmdcore.c[0m defines the operations plus three exported helpers; [38;5;10mmdmain.c[0m is the driver.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;252m[1m## Rust layout ([38;5;10mtranslation/[0m)[0m[0m
[0m[0m
- [38;5;10msrc/mdmacros.rs[0m — the header's preprocessor logic as [38;5;10m#[cfg(feature = …)][0m-gated constants ([38;5;10mOP[0m, [38;5;10mOP_NAME[0m, [38;5;10mREPEAT[0m, [38;5;10mINIT[0m) and functions ([38;5;10mstep_op[0m, [38;5;10mrep[0m, [38;5;10mrun_loop[0m, [38;5;10mdispatch_rep[0m, [38;5;10mdo_loop[0m).[0m[0m
- [38;5;10msrc/mdcore.rs[0m — [38;5;10mop_add[0m/[38;5;10mop_sub[0m/[38;5;10mop_mul[0m, the private [38;5;10maccum_<OP>[0m, the [38;5;10mG_OP[0m/[38;5;10mG_OP_NAME[0m globals, and [38;5;10mhelper_call[0m/[38;5;10mhelper_ptr[0m/[38;5;10muse_generated[0m, all [38;5;10m#[unsafe(no_mangle)] extern "C"[0m. No namespace macros exist in this project, so the source names are already the final linker symbols.[0m[0m
- [38;5;10msrc/lib.rs[0m — [38;5;10mcdylib[0m crate root re-exporting the C surface.[0m[0m
- [38;5;10msrc/main.rs[0m — the [38;5;10mdriver[0m binary. Since the lib is [38;5;10mcdylib[0m-only it cannot be linked by the bin, so [38;5;10mmain.rs[0m compiles the same two modules directly, matching how CMake compiles both [38;5;10m.c[0m files into [38;5;10mdriver[0m.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;252m[1m## Features[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;10madd[0m/[38;5;10msub[0m/[38;5;10mmul[0m for [38;5;10mOP[0m, and [38;5;10m"0"[0m…[38;5;10m"7"[0m for [38;5;10mREPEAT[0m — the CMake cache [3mvalues[23m, lowercased. Readable aliases ([38;5;10mop_mul[0m, [38;5;10mrepeat_7[0m) just enable the canonical feature. [38;5;10mdefault = [][0m reproduces the header's [38;5;10m#ifndef[0m fallbacks (add, 5), so plain [38;5;10mcargo build[0m equals a plain [38;5;10mcmake[0m configure, and explicit selection is never ambiguous. When conflicting values are enabled the cfg cascade still yields exactly one definition, so [38;5;10m--all-features[0m compiles.[0m[0m
